shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"YnhrJ94quRechwC3a7Pd-g","review_id":"-fyLfVB-yM1In5jJCW5-rQ","date":"2016-06-25T18:42:46","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9334063529968262,"text_excerpt":"Our dining experience was a real trip down memory lane. I loved seeing the old ( and new ) artwork in the foyer, bar and dining room. The ambience and service ( Brett) was wonderful. The food reminded me of other local restaurants ( I guess John Besh)-- the Parkerhouse rolls with sea salt, the lightly fried oysters, and the stuffed squash blossoms with pickled vegetables (mmm - delicious). The crab remick was a Pontchartrain throwback- very good as well as the Mile High Pie. While the pie as good, it would be even better if it was more like the original - a regular pie crust and much more meringue. The pecan pie was only ok. The restaurant needs its distinctive cuisine- maybe it could be ..."},{"business_id":"YnhrJ94quRechwC3a7Pd-g","review_id":"NfR-h7oU6YkwIGSzpuCE0A","date":"2016-11-18T18:32:53","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9275228977203369,"text_excerpt":"I don't think I was born yet back in the Caribbean rooms original heyday, but I can say if it was anything now like it was then I know why people loved it. Reservations have been hard to come by and I understand why. We had to have the early bird special in order to get in. The decor is some of the most interesting I think I've seen. It almost seemed silly mixed with the formal atmosphere you feel there. Our waiter was great. He had an old New Orleans accent that reminded me of my uncles. He has great recommendations. I had the soft shell crab dish. It was perfect. Light and crisply fried. I had been jonesing for soft shell crab and this delivered. I had an appetizer, but I don't remember..."},{"business_id":"YnhrJ94quRechwC3a7Pd-g","review_id":"HINDh-Mr6i4ENNv2cJ723g","date":"2018-02-25T00:12:50","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9270435571670532,"text_excerpt":"I love the history entrenched in this place, especially since my parents dined here when they were dating and were sad to hear when it initially closed. A classy destination decades ago, this revival of the Caribbean Room maintained the elegant ambiance of a bygone era, but gave the menu a respectful face lift - dining here feels like being transported to a lost time when dining was an experience with white gloves and glamour (but also now with a dash of Lil' Wayne). Corbin, our waiter was affable and available - he built a relationship and rapport with us that is lost at most modern restaurants. The food held it's own too, not fading in the shadow of the atmosphere. Started with the shri..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"YnhrJ94quRechwC3a7Pd-g","photo_id":"eWAVpM7p4R8ipQ7uViZ0pA","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/eWAVpM7p4R8ipQ7uViZ0pA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8636273145675659},{"business_id":"YnhrJ94quRechwC3a7Pd-g","photo_id":"w0tDRZE2g-Ymrg2Sm0G2lA","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/w0tDRZE2g-Ymrg2Sm0G2lA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8112472295761108},{"business_id":"YnhrJ94quRechwC3a7Pd-g","photo_id":"SlQJQPGbVI4Uha_99A-ujw","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/SlQJQPGbVI4Uha_99A-ujw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7568449974060059},{"business_id":"YnhrJ94quRechwC3a7Pd-g","photo_id":"MVbGj7HtBHIHnZ_lxTEdSw","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/MVbGj7HtBHIHnZ_lxTEdSw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7551778554916382},{"business_id":"YnhrJ94quRechwC3a7Pd-g","photo_id":"BjFCaTObLj